    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00004",
      "segmentId": "m00125:para:para-00004"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00002",
      "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00125:caption:fig-00002-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00125:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "2-bromo-2-methylpropane undergoes a 3-step reaction to form neutral alcohol and hydronium by way of a carbocation. Step 1 forms carbocation, is rate-limiting; step 2 quenches carbocation, is fast."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_11_04_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00005",
      "segmentId": "m00125:para:para-00005"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00003",
      "class": "scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00125:caption:fig-00003-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00125:alt:fig-00003-alt",
          "text": "An energy diagram shows a large barrier to step 1 of S N 1 (forming carbocation) and small barrier to step 2 (quenching carbocation)."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_11_04_003.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00006",
      "segmentId": "m00125:para:para-00006"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00004",
      "class": "scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00125:caption:fig-00004-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00125:alt:fig-00004-alt",
          "text": "The reaction is represented using ball-and-stick model. Chiral substrate undergoes dissociation to form a planar, achiral carbocation intermediate, which reacts with nucleophile to produce 50% inversion or 50% retention of configurations."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_11_04_004.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00007",
      "segmentId": "m00125:para:para-00007"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00005",
      "class": "unnumbered",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00125:alt:fig-00005-alt",
          "text": "A reaction of (R)-6-chloro-2,6-dimethyloctane with water and ethanol, forms two products with 60% S (inversion) and 40% R (retention), respectively."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_11_04_005.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00008",
      "segmentId": "m00125:para:para-00008"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00006",
      "class": "scaled-down",
      "caption": {
        "segmentId": "m00125:caption:fig-00006-caption"
      },
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00125:alt:fig-00006-alt",
          "text": "The reaction is represented using ball-and-stick model. Chiral substrate undergoes dissociation to form intermediates and yields two products by racemization (from free carbocation) and one product by inversion (from ion pair)."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_11_04_006.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
